[[:db/retract 17592186314298 :answer-field/choices 17592186313531] [:db/retract 17592186164803 :answer-field/choices 17592186164805] [:db/retract 17592186164803 :answer-field/choices 17592186164807] [:db/retract 17592186164797 :answer-field/choices 17592186164800] [:db/retract 17592186164797 :answer-field/choices 17592186164801] [:db/retract 17592186164797 :answer-field/choices 17592186164802] [:db/retract 17592186164797 :answer-field/choices 17592186164798] [:db/retract 17592186164797 :answer-field/choices 17592186164799] [:db/retract 17592186314685 :answer-field/choices 17592186312963] [:db/retract 17592186314544 :answer-field/choices 17592186312718] [:db/retract 17592186314293 :answer-field/choices 17592186313346] {:db/id 17592186167266 :question/problem "Consider the boundary value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+4{\\lambda }^{2}y=0,\\,y(0)=y(1)=0,\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\lambda \\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the parameter values corresponding to the eigenvalues and the associated eigenfunctions of this problem.\n\n$\\,$ The eigenvalues correspond to the parameter values ${\\lambda }_{n}=$ {{field-1}}, where $n\\in N.$\n\n$\\,$ The eigenfunctions are ${y}_{n}(x)=$ {{field-2}}, where ${B}_{n}\\in R.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186314298 :answer-field/correct 17592186313310 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167268 :question/problem "Consider the boundary value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-8\\lambda {y}^{′}+16{\\lambda }^{2}y=0,\\,y(0)=0,\\,y(1)+{y}^{′}(1)=0,\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\lambda \\in R.\n$$\n\nFind the eigenvalues and eigenfunctions of this problem. Assume that $B$ and $C$ are constants.\n\n$\\,$ The eigenvalues are $\\lambda =$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The eigenfunctions are $y=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We consider the cases $\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda \\ne 0$ separately, since they correspond to different solutions. \n\n**Case 1**: First, we consider $\\lambda =0.$ \n\nSetting $\\lambda =0$ gives the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=0.\n$$\n\nIntegrating this equation gives\n\n$$\ny=Ax+B.\n$$\n\nApplying the conditions $y(0)=0$ and $y(1)+{y}^{′}(1)=0$ yields the trivial solution $y≡0.$ Since the zero solution is not an eigenfunction, $\\lambda =0$ is not an eigenvalue.\n\n**Case 2**: Next, we consider $\\lambda \\ne 0.$\n\nTo find the fundamental solutions, we set $y={e}^{mx}.$ The auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}-8\\lambda m+16{\\lambda }^{2} & =0 \\\\ (m-4\\lambda )(m-4\\lambda ) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the double root $m=4\\lambda .$ So, the fundamental solutions are \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(x)={e}^{4\\lambda x},\\,{y}_{2}(x)=x{e}^{4\\lambda x}\n$$\n\nand the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{4\\lambda x}+Bx{e}^{4\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nApplying the boundary condition $y(0)=0$ yields\n\n$$\nA+B\\cdot 0=0\n$$\n\nwhich gives $A=0.$ So, we have\n\n$$\ny=Bx{e}^{4\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}=B{e}^{4\\lambda x}+4B\\lambda x{e}^{4\\lambda x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the boundary condition $y(1)+{y}^{′}(1)=0$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B{e}^{4\\lambda }+B{e}^{4\\lambda }+4B\\lambda {e}^{4\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ 2B{e}^{4\\lambda }+4B\\lambda {e}^{4\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ B{e}^{4\\lambda }+2B\\lambda {e}^{4\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ B{e}^{4\\lambda }(1+2\\lambda ) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor nontrivial solutions, we require $B\\ne 0.$ Thus, since ${e}^{4\\lambda }>0,$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\lambda =-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding eigenfunction is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =Bx{e}^{4\\lambda x} \\\\  & =Bx{e}^{-2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164803 :answer-field/correct 17592186164806 :answer-field/choices ["answer-a1488815-d1a6-5503-a380-473f0f85b5d7" "answer-e8d41e3c-6c2e-5718-8ed2-cbf24e5e3949"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1488815-d1a6-5503-a380-473f0f85b5d7" :answer/id #uuid "a1488815-d1a6-5503-a380-473f0f85b5d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8d41e3c-6c2e-5718-8ed2-cbf24e5e3949" :answer/id #uuid "e8d41e3c-6c2e-5718-8ed2-cbf24e5e3949" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186164797 :answer-field/correct "answer-7708b0c3-fc6f-5c9e-b153-91f22444d86e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7708b0c3-fc6f-5c9e-b153-91f22444d86e" "answer-e321edcb-caed-5e92-a02b-54c8f1f87eb9" "answer-858b6a2d-f127-50fb-b974-fcb22a273b64" "answer-ad35330a-43cf-5531-8b67-e32f2b60d443" "answer-b965e478-138a-5a0a-89f2-8c72e03c9a3f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7708b0c3-fc6f-5c9e-b153-91f22444d86e" :answer/id #uuid "7708b0c3-fc6f-5c9e-b153-91f22444d86e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Bx{e}^{-2x}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e321edcb-caed-5e92-a02b-54c8f1f87eb9" :answer/id #uuid "e321edcb-caed-5e92-a02b-54c8f1f87eb9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Bx{e}^{-x}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-858b6a2d-f127-50fb-b974-fcb22a273b64" :answer/id #uuid "858b6a2d-f127-50fb-b974-fcb22a273b64" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Bx{e}^{2x}$ and $Cx{e}^{-2x}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad35330a-43cf-5531-8b67-e32f2b60d443" :answer/id #uuid "ad35330a-43cf-5531-8b67-e32f2b60d443" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Bx{e}^{2x}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b965e478-138a-5a0a-89f2-8c72e03c9a3f" :answer/id #uuid "b965e478-138a-5a0a-89f2-8c72e03c9a3f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Bx{e}^{x}$ and $Cx{e}^{-x}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167269 :question/problem "Consider the boundary value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-8\\lambda {y}^{′}+16{\\lambda }^{2}y=0,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=0,\\,y(2)+2{y}^{′}(2)=0,\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\lambda \\in R.\n$$\n\nFind the eigenvalues and eigenfunctions of this problem. Assume that $B$ and $C$ are constants.\n\n$\\,$ The eigenvalues are $\\lambda =$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The eigenfunctions are $y=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We consider the cases $\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda \\ne 0$ separately, since they correspond to different solutions. \n\n**Case 1**: First, we consider $\\lambda =0.$ \n\nSetting $\\lambda =0$ gives the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=0.\n$$\n\nIntegrating this equation gives\n\n$$\ny=Ax+B.\n$$\n\nApplying the conditions ${y}^{′}(1)=0$ and $y(2)+2{y}^{′}(2)=0$ yields the trivial solution $y≡0.$ Since the zero solution is not an eigenfunction, $\\lambda =0$ is not an eigenvalue.\n\n**Case 2**: Next, we consider $\\lambda \\ne 0.$\n\nTo find the fundamental solutions, we set $y={e}^{mx}.$ The auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}-8\\lambda m+16{\\lambda }^{2} & =0 \\\\ (m-4\\lambda )(m-4\\lambda ) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the double root $m=4\\lambda .$ So, the fundamental solutions are \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(x)={e}^{4\\lambda x},\\,{y}_{2}(x)=x{e}^{4\\lambda x}\n$$\n\nand the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{4\\lambda x}+Bx{e}^{4\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =4A\\lambda {e}^{4\\lambda x}+B{e}^{4\\lambda x}+4B\\lambda x{e}^{4\\lambda x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the boundary condition ${y}^{′}(1)=0$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4A\\lambda {e}^{4\\lambda }+B{e}^{4\\lambda }+4B\\lambda {e}^{4\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ 4A\\lambda +B+4B\\lambda  & =0 \\\\ (4\\lambda )A+(1+4\\lambda )B & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the boundary condition $y(2)+2{y}^{′}(2)=0$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{e}^{8\\lambda }+2B{e}^{8\\lambda }+2(4A\\lambda {e}^{8\\lambda }+B{e}^{8\\lambda }+8B\\lambda {e}^{8\\lambda }) & =0 \\\\ A+2B+2(4A\\lambda +B+8B\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ A+2B+8A\\lambda +2B+16B\\lambda  & =0 \\\\ (1+8\\lambda )A+(4+16\\lambda )B & =0 \\\\ (1+8\\lambda )A+4(1+4\\lambda )B & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following systems of equations for $A$ and $B:$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(4\\lambda )A+(1+4\\lambda )B=0 \\\\ (1+8\\lambda )A+4(1+4\\lambda )B=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis homogeneous linear system has a nontrivial solution if and only if the determinant is zero. This gives\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}4\\lambda  & 1+4\\lambda  \\\\ 1+8\\lambda  & 4(1+4\\lambda )\\end{aligned}|=0.\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\lambda \\cdot 4(1+4\\lambda )-(1+4\\lambda )(1+8\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (1+4\\lambda )[16\\lambda -(1+8\\lambda )] & =0 \\\\ (1+4\\lambda )[16\\lambda -1-8\\lambda ] & =0 \\\\ (1+4\\lambda )(8\\lambda -1) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=-\\frac{1}{4}\\text{ and }{\\lambda }_{2}=\\frac{1}{8}.$\n\nFinally, we find the eigenfunction corresponding to each eigenvalue:\n\n- Consider ${\\lambda }_{1}=-\\frac{1}{4}.$ Then, we have the solution\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}(x) & =A{e}^{4{\\lambda }_{1}x}+Bx{e}^{4{\\lambda }_{1}x} \\\\  & =A{e}^{-x}+Bx{e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand substituting ${\\lambda }_{1}$ into\n\n$$\n(4\\lambda )A+(1+4\\lambda )B=0\n$$\n\n \nwe get \n\n$$\n-A+(1-1)B=0\n$$\n\n \nwhich gives $A=0,$ and where $B$ is a free parameter. Thus, the eigenfunction corresponding to this eigenvalue is\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(x)=Bx{e}^{-x}.\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=\\frac{1}{8},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}(x) & =A{e}^{4{\\lambda }_{2}x}+Bx{e}^{4{\\lambda }_{2}x} \\\\  & =A{e}^{x/2}+Bx{e}^{x/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand substituting ${\\lambda }_{2}$ into\n\n$$\n(4\\lambda )A+(1+4\\lambda )B=0\n$$\n\n \nwe get \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}A+\\frac{3}{2}B=0\\,⇒\\,A=-3B\n$$\n\nwhere $B$ is a free parameter. Thus, the eigenfunction corresponding to this eigenvalue is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}(x) & =-3B{e}^{x/2}+Bx{e}^{x/2} \\\\  & =B{e}^{x/2}(x-3) \\\\  & =C{e}^{x/2}(x-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we have set $C=B.$\n\nSo, the eigenfunctions corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ respectively, are $Bx{e}^{-x}\\text{ and }C{e}^{x/2}(x-3).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186314685 :answer-field/correct 17592186312220 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186314544 :answer-field/correct 17592186312759 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186314745 :question/problem "Consider the boundary value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+9\\lambda y=0,\\,y(0)={y}^{′}(2)=0,\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\lambda \\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the parameter values corresponding to the eigenvalues and the associated eigenfunctions of this problem.\n\n$\\,$ The eigenvalues correspond to the parameter values ${\\lambda }_{n}=$ {{field-1}}, where $n\\in {N}_{0}.$\n\n$\\,$ The eigenfunctions are ${y}_{n}(x)=$ {{field-2}}, where ${B}_{n}\\in R.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186314293 :answer-field/correct 17592186313779 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186391709 :question/problem "Consider the boundary value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+16\\lambda y=0,\\,y(0)=y(5)=0,\\,0\\le x\\le 5,\\,\\lambda \\ge 0.\n$$\n\nFind the parameter values corresponding to the eigenvalues and the associated eigenfunctions of this problem.\n\n$\\,$ The eigenvalues correspond to the parameter values ${\\lambda }_{n}=$ {{field-1}}, where $n\\in N.$\n\n$\\,$ The eigenfunctions are ${y}_{n}(x)=$ {{field-2}}, where ${B}_{n}\\in R.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-fa9d4c91-2ac2-50a9-bf17-b5e5e2265182" :activity/id #uuid "fa9d4c91-2ac2-50a9-bf17-b5e5e2265182" :activity/title "Eigenvalues and Eigenfunctions of Homogeneous BVPs" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049830 :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-fa5303a7-7edf-519b-8a8a-d599ebe59258" "step-f1e042a8-1faa-5865-8d30-e1ea1fe82b24" "step-f8b73451-fda1-5086-8156-fc15d81c7a88" "step-1cab76e5-6c1e-514f-a717-d9c42a4499b0" "step-8a1cfa99-80c5-51a8-869c-32eec8bcaf70"] :activity/first-step "step-fa5303a7-7edf-519b-8a8a-d599ebe59258" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-fa5303a7-7edf-519b-8a8a-d599ebe59258" :step/id #uuid "fa5303a7-7edf-519b-8a8a-d599ebe59258" :step/content 17592186167266 :step/next "step-f1e042a8-1faa-5865-8d30-e1ea1fe82b24" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f1e042a8-1faa-5865-8d30-e1ea1fe82b24" :step/id #uuid "f1e042a8-1faa-5865-8d30-e1ea1fe82b24" :step/content 17592186167268 :step/next "step-f8b73451-fda1-5086-8156-fc15d81c7a88" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f8b73451-fda1-5086-8156-fc15d81c7a88" :step/id #uuid "f8b73451-fda1-5086-8156-fc15d81c7a88" :step/content 17592186167269 :step/next "step-1cab76e5-6c1e-514f-a717-d9c42a4499b0" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-1cab76e5-6c1e-514f-a717-d9c42a4499b0" :step/id #uuid "1cab76e5-6c1e-514f-a717-d9c42a4499b0" :step/content 17592186314745 :step/next "step-8a1cfa99-80c5-51a8-869c-32eec8bcaf70" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-8a1cfa99-80c5-51a8-869c-32eec8bcaf70" :step/id #uuid "8a1cfa99-80c5-51a8-869c-32eec8bcaf70" :step/content 17592186391709 :db/ensure [:step/validate]}]
